# The app runs entirely as the Next.js web app in `apps/web`, which talks to its
# own API routes on the same origin — so there is nothing to configure here.
#
# Server-side configuration lives in Vercel's project settings (or in
# `apps/web/.env.local` for local development):
#
#   DATABASE_URL    – Neon Postgres, the pooled endpoint (host contains "-pooler")
#   JWT_SECRET      – signs session tokens
#   GEMINI_API_KEY  – optional; enables the AI coach and the journal scan
#
# See apps/web/README.md. This file is kept as a pointer to that, since the repo
# root used to hold EXPO_PUBLIC_SYNC_URL back when a React Native app shipped
# alongside the web one.
